DECLARE Mixed HAS
    out  IS A NUMBER
    note IS A STRING

GIVEN v1 IS A NUMBER
      v2 IS A STRING
GIVETH A Mixed
mkMixed v1 v2 MEANS Mixed WITH
    out  IS v1
    note IS v2

-- dmnmd: table "Mixed", column "out": (EXPONENT share 0.5). L4 computes a power with a negative, fractional or non-literal exponent in binary floating point, where dmnmd's own evaluator refuses a fractional exponent and rounds a negative one to 34 digits (D-1), so the two can differ.
-- dmnmd: table "Mixed", column "out": (EXPONENT amt (0 - 1)). L4 computes a power with a negative, fractional or non-literal exponent in binary floating point, where dmnmd's own evaluator refuses a fractional exponent and rounds a negative one to 34 digits (D-1), so the two can differ.
GIVEN amt   IS A NUMBER
      share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Mixed
Mixed amt share MEANS
  BRANCH
    IF amt < 0             THEN mkMixed (amt / 4) "a"
    IF          share > 10 THEN mkMixed (EXPONENT share 0.5) "b"
    OTHERWISE mkMixed (EXPONENT amt (0 - 1)) "c"

